  "text": "Added duration limit enforcement to Blossom video upload system:\n\n**Files Modified:**\n1. `src/streaming/bunny-webhook.mjs` - Added duration check in `handleVideoEncoded()`, stores `duration-rejected:*` in KV\n2. `src/index.mjs` - Added duration check in `handleGetBlob()` and .m3u8 endpoint handler\n3. `src/streaming/playback-resolver.mjs` - Added duration check in `resolveUrl()` to block all playback\n\n**Key Details:**\n- User-facing limit: 6 seconds\n- Actual enforcement: 7 seconds (tolerance)\n- Rejection stored in KV: `duration-rejected:{sha256}`\n- Error response: HTTP 400 with helpful message\n- Videos kept in BunnyStream, just blocked from serving\n\n**Testing Notes:**\n- Need to test with video > 7 seconds to verify webhook rejection\n- Check all serving paths: direct GET, HLS .m3u8, PlaybackResolver\n- Verify error message is helpful for users",
  "sections": [
    "Project Notes"
  ],
